AArch64 GussetParkWakeDekkerDisproofLDAPR
"Disproof companion (`Sometimes`) to `park_wake_dekker.litmus`:
 replaces the reader's `SWPAL` + `LDAR` with `STLR` (`W & L`) + FEAT_LRCPC
 `LDAPR` (`R & Q`, RCpc acquire-pc).

 Under `aarch64hwreqs.cat`, `bob` orders `[Exp & W & L]; po; [Exp & R & A]`
 (`STLR` -> `LDAR`), NOT `[Exp & W & L]; po; [Exp & R & Q]` (`STLR` -> `LDAPR`).
 Consequently, `0:X2=0 /\ 1:X4=0` (lost wake) is architecturally permitted!

 Expected `herd7` verdict under `aarch64.cat`: `Sometimes`."
{
  uint64_t seq = 0;
  uint32_t waiting = 0;
  0:X0=1; 0:X1=seq; 0:X3=waiting;
  1:X0=1; 1:X1=waiting; 1:X3=seq;
}
 P0                       | P1                       ;
 STLR X0, [X1]            | STLR W0, [X1]            ;
 DMB ISH                  | LDAPR X4, [X3]           ;
 LDR W2, [X3]             |                          ;
exists (0:X2=0 /\ 1:X4=0)
